+/*
+ * Hi3798CV200 VDP video-layer scaler (ZME) coefficient memory.
+ *
+ * The VDP ZME is the same IP family as the VPSS ZME: the community histb-vpss
+ * driver (patch 0008) already drives it on this hardware, so its filter tables
+ * and its 10-bit / 16-bit packing are reused here.  The vendor VDP path gets
+ * its tables from the closed PQ library (DRV_PQ_GetVdpZmeCoef), so the VDP
+ * packing itself is [inferred] to be identical - NOT seen on hardware.
+ *
+ * At exactly 1:1 the layer runs the scaler with every FIR in copy mode (the
+ * way the BSP VPSS port does) and these tables are never consulted, except for
+ * the vertical chroma FIR that turns 4:2:0 chroma into 4:2:2.
